{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And He said.</b> The first sign is the staff, which was already in his hand; the second, in his hand. Yefet said: because He suspected that they would not believe, his hand was stricken with leprosy — if so, this should have been the first sign. Rabbi Yeshuah said that this is an allusion to Israel, who were at first free; HaShem afflicted them with Egyptian servitude, and He will heal them and they will return free." "<b>And He said.</b> The Gaon [Saadia] said that החיק is the part of the arm [i.e., the fold], and thus: בחיקו ישא (Isaiah 40:11), שאהו בחיקך (Numbers 12). And others said that it is the garment adjacent to the chest."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:26.639632364Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}